  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Complimenting Borana PBF project to further improve MCH services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention will target 25 health facilities in Borana between April 2022 and September 2022 and will be implemented in complementarity with the PBF project in Borana. The intervention will address the following categories of activities with detailed activities shown in the Gantt chart in section 3:
1.	Capacity building of Health workers and regulators on BEmONC and IMNCI
2.	Infrastructure Rehabilitation
3.	Provision of basic medical equipment
4.	Improved nutrition of under-5 children and pregnant mothers
5.	Improved coverage of fully immunized children
6.	Improve WASH facilities
7.	Monitoring, Evaluation, and Learning</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this PBF complimentary project is to further strengthen the health system in the 25 selected health facilities in Borana to provide better quality of MCH services. More specifically, the PBF complimentary project will:
1.	Equip Health Facilities with essential medical equipment for MCH services. 
2.	Strengthen immunization outreach services in the Borana Zone.
3.	Strengthen the Capacity of midwives on Basic Newborn and Obstetric Care (BEmNOC). 
4.	Increase the availability of food at Health Facilities for distribution to pregnant mothers in the waiting mothers&#x2019; homes.
5.	Increase the availability of WASH facilities at selected Health Facilities with water supply challenges. 
6.	Improve infrastructure of maternity and EPI rooms at selected Health Facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen the health system in the Borana Zone of Oromia regional state, Cordaid Ethiopia has been implementing performance-based financing (PBF) program in 48 health facilities found in fourteen (14) pastoralist woredas. This project has been under implementation since 2015 GC, starting with 9 health facilities in the first phase and expanding to cover the entire zone by July 2021. So far promising success had been obtained in all health facilities in terms of improving health service delivery and quality. 
While the current PBF project has contributed to the health system strengthening in Borana, there are certain aspects that are still not sufficiently addressed. These include infrastructural and medical equipment needs. These investments need substantial financial resources which most health facilities cannot afford using their regular limited subsidies. This has resulted in stagnation in quality improvement as they continuously lose score/subsidies on these gaps. Based on this, Coraid Ethiopia in collaboration with Cordaid Global Office fundraising team produced a documentary which focused on maternal and child health care in Borana. The documentary was then used to fundraise in the Netherlands resulting in an additional budget. Since the funding was generated through a documentary filmed in Borana, the funds will be invested in Borana health facilities to complement the existing performance-based financing (PBF) project to further improve the quality of maternal and child health care.</narrative>
  </description>
